From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Admit the J714s in developer builds through a
 developer-only sealed catalog

apple,j714s (MacBook Pro 14-inch M5 Pro, T6050) becomes a developer board in
scripts/supported-models.json, marked untested: no channel catalog may list
it, and check-catalog still rejects it. make-unsigned-catalog.py gains
--developer-only for a developer build that installs only developer boards:
every listed board must be one, the supported-Mac coverage rule does not
apply, and each developer board's model carries its manifest note as
previewNote. MacModelNames names the J714s.

Nothing in the app refuses the J714s outside the catalog (only apple,j614s is
explicitly refused), and the pinned engine already inspects j714sap
(T6050, board 0x08) as supported, so no gating change is needed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
